      "narrative": null,
      "content": "This paper presents a specialized methodology for digitizing and\nsegmenting mathematical documents from zbMATH Open, a com-\nprehensive database of mathematical literature, to enhance ma-\nchine processing capabilities. Currently, approximately 831,000\ndocuments exist only in scanned volumes, which makes them not\nmachine-processable. Furthermore, these scans often span multi-\nple pages or share pages with other documents and incorporate\ndiverse typesetting techniques, posing challenges for automated\nprocessing.\nTo address these issues, we evaluate various Optical Charac-\nter Recognition (OCR) to",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Summarizes a pipeline for digitizing and segmenting ~831,000 scanned mathematical documents in zbMATH Open using Mathpix for LaTeX OCR and fine-tuned generative LLMs in a Majority Voting framework for document separation, achieving 97.5% text extraction accuracy (89.1% boundary index accuracy overall) and processing 810,977 documents into machine-readable text (721,288 with LaTeX boundary indexes).",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
